        'A. Introduction\nWe recognize that your privacy is important and we take it seriously. Your privacy and trust are important to us, and we are committed to being transparent about the use of the information we collect. \nThis Privacy Policy describes TrainDriver\'s policies and procedures regarding the collection, use, disclosure and sharing of your personal information or personal data when you access or use our Website, Applications and/or Services. \nPlease note that TrainDriver\'s terms of service apply to this privacy policy. By accessing or using the TrainDriver - 91免费版 website and applications, you agree to accept this Privacy Policy unconditionally. If you do not agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not use the TrainDriver - 91免费版 service. \nThis privacy policy is important. We hope you will take the time to read it carefully. \nB. Age Restrictions\n TrainDriver - 91免费版 is not suitable for children. maxLines: Children under the age of 12 are not permitted to use our Site, Applications and/or Services for any purpose. TrainDriver - The 91免费版 will never knowingly solicit or accept personally identifiable information or other content from users or visitors who the TrainDriver - The 91免费版 knows are under the age of 12. If TrainDriver - 91免费版 discovers that a user under 12 years of age has created an account, or that a user or visitor under 12 years of age has posted personally identifiable information or other content to the Service, TrainDriver - 91免费版 will terminate the account and delete that information or Other content content. \nUsers between the ages of 12 and 18 (each a "Youth") may not access or use the Services unless (i) the Teen and his or her parent or legal guardian first agree to these Terms of Service; or an account established under the supervision of a guardian and with the permission of a parent or guardian. If you allow a teenager to use the Services, you hereby agree to these Terms of Service on behalf of yourself and the teenager. You further agree that you are solely responsible for any and all use of the Services by your children, whether or not such use is authorized by you. \nC. Data Collection\nWe want you to understand the types of information we collect when you use our Services. We use this information to operate, develop and improve our service - from figuring out basic things like what language you speak, to more complex information like which ads you find most useful, what\'s most important to you online Author or stories you might like. \nWhen you interact with our Sites, Applications and/or Services, we collect information that can be used to identify you ("Personal Data"). Some of the information we collect is stored in a way that cannot be linked back to you (“Non-Personal Data”). \nWhen you log in, we collect the information stored in your account (usually your nickname, email address, and account password), which we treat as personal information. This log information may include, but is not limited to, your Internet Protocol address, browser type, browser language, the date and time of your query, and cookie data. If you log into TrainDriver - 91免费版 using social network credentials (such as a third-party account), we will request permission to access basic information from that account, such as your name and email address. You can stop sharing this information with us at any time by removing TrainDriver - 91免费版 access to the account. When you are not logged in to our Services, we store the information we collect using unique identifiers associated with the application and device you are using. This collection helps us do things like maintain your language preferences across browsing sessions. \nIf you are a paying customer, we will collect your payment information. This information is required to complete commercial transactions on our apps and websites. We use this information to enable and complete your transactions. If you choose to use the services of any third party to complete your order and pay, you will provide your credit card number directly to the third party. The third party\'s privacy policy will apply to the information you provide on their website. \nIf you choose to participate in our surveys, we may ask you to provide certain information (including personal data and non-personal data), which will be used to provide personalized help and instructions. \nThe information we collect and how it is used depends on how you use our services and how you manage your privacy controls. \nD. Use of your data\nTrainDriver - 91免费版 uses your data where necessary for the performance of our contract with you and for our legitimate business interests. Your data is processed and used for the following purposes:\nTo help us provide and manage our website, applications and/or services, to authenticate users for security purposes, to provide personalized user features and access, to process transactions , conduct research, develop new features, and improve our functionality, algorithms, and usability of our Site, Applications, and/or Services. \nTo communicate with you about your use of our Sites, Applications and/or Services, product announcements and software updates, and to respond to your requests for assistance, including providing account verification support if you encounter difficulty accessing your account. \nSend you direct marketing information and special offers about our products and services via inbox messages. If you do not want to receive any of the above messages, please contact us through customer service when you create your account or any time thereafter. \nDisplay User Content associated with your account and ensure that it is available when you use our Services. \nCompute aggregate statistics on the number of unique devices using our Site, Applications and/or Services and detect and prevent fraud and abuse of these devices. \nAnalyze what features or actions are taken on our website, applications and/or services to improve your experience. \nVerify the consent of parents and guardians for minors to use TrainDriver - 91免费版 through the payment process. \nTo facilitate your purchases on our website, applications and/or services, and to verify your real name to facilitate the creation of your payment account. \nUse a third-party payment platform to process your payment. \nFor example, we will know how many users visited specific pages on the website and which links they clicked. We use this aggregate information to better understand and optimize the website. \nIf you choose to use our services or provide us with your information, your information may be transferred to servers or databases located outside your country or jurisdiction (including Singapore) and stored in those servers or databases. for handling and maintenance. The laws in these countries may not be as forward-looking as the country where you live. If you do not want your information to be transferred to, processed or maintained outside your country or jurisdiction, you should not use our Site, Applications and/or Services. \nE. Cookies\nWe use cookies to provide, protect and promote our products. \nA "cookie" is a small file containing a string of characters that is sent to your computer when you visit a website. Cookies can remain on your device for varying periods of time. Some cookies are "session cookies," which means they only exist while your browser or application is open. These will be automatically deleted once you close the browser or application. Other cookies are "persistent cookies," which means they survive after your browser or application is closed. The service can use cookies to recognize your device when you open and use the service again. \nWe use cookies to improve the quality of our service and to better understand how people interact with us. We use cookies to:\nVerify login information. \nTrack service-related traffic flow and travel patterns. \nUnderstand the total number of visitors and device types that continue to access the service. \nMonitor the performance of the service and continuously improve it. \nCustomize and enhance your online experience. \nProvide you with customer service. \nYou have the right to choose whether to accept cookies. However, please note that if you choose to reject cookies, you may not be able to use the full functionality of the Services. \nMost devices (for mobile apps) and browsers (for web apps and pages) are initially set up to accept cookies and allow you to change your cookie settings. These settings can usually be found in your browser\'s Options or Preferences menu. You can reset your browser to refuse all cookies or to indicate when a cookie is being sent. \nF. Information Sharing\na. Information shared on our Sites, Apps and/or Services\n Any information you include in your publicly visible TrainDriver profile, which may include your Profile ID , nickname, photo and your bio, will be shared on our Sites, Applications and/or Services to maintain your account and requirements in accordance with your instructions. \nb. Sharing your data outside our Sites, Apps and/or Services\nSome features related to TrainDriver - 91免费版 allow you to provide shared information to people outside the TrainDriver - 91免费版 network. For example, publicly accessible blogs and forums, or certain social media features in TrainDriver - such as "plug-ins" (which create a direct link between two websites) allow you to republish and disclose shared information. If you share information using these features, third parties not affiliated with us may be able to see and use it. \nThe information we share with such third parties is as described to you when you first use the service or feature, and we require third parties to provide the same or equivalent user data protection as described in this policy. You can control which third parties have access to this information in your account. You may revoke your consent to the sharing of this information at any time by following the instructions listed here. Please note that if you ask us not to share this information with third parties, you may no longer be able to use that service or feature. We are not responsible for any third party\'s use of any information you provide to them. \nWe will not rent or sell your personal information to others unless we obtain your consent. We will only disclose your personal information to other companies, organizations and individuals under the following circumstances described in this policy:\nIf there is an acquisition, merger or merger of our website, applications and/or services or our company or purchasable parts or sold, we may transfer your personal information to relevant third parties (for example, acquirers, merging parties, etc.). We will make every effort to protect your privacy rights by providing reasonable notice to you (e.g., through prominent announcements on our Site, Apps and/or Services). In this case, your account information may be transferred to the new company, but it will still be subject to the terms of this policy. \nIt is necessary for us to share this information to: (i) comply with applicable laws, court orders or government requests; (ii) prevent fraud or other illegal activities; (iii) protect the rights and property of TrainDriver - 91免费版s; ( iv) enforce our terms and conditions; (v) prevent physical damage; (vi) investigate suspected or actual illegal activity; or (vii) ensure TrainDriver\'s compliance. This may include providing information to public authorities (including law enforcement agencies). \nG. Data Security\nTrainDriver - 91免费版 takes reasonable security measures to protect your information from loss, misuse, unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration or destruction. Although we take reasonable steps to protect your information, please be aware that the Internet is never a secure transmission platform and we cannot guarantee the security of information you send through our Services. \nH. Information About Rights\nYou can ask us to delete your account at any time. We will retain your personal data for a period of time in accordance with applicable law. For example, we may retain your account information to prevent fraud and abuse, or for tax, accounting, or legal requirements. In this case, we mark your account as "inactive" and save it in our database. We will not delete your account to avoid all information related to your account related to our services. \nYou can ask us to stop sending you marketing emails or other direct marketing messages at any time. \nIf you have any questions or concerns about the information we collect, please feel free to contact us through customer service. \nI. Information about the legal basis\nWe have your consent, which means that you have agreed to us processing your personal data in order to achieve a specific purpose; or we need to process your personal data in order to perform our contract with you , such as when you register an account on our website; or we must comply with a legal obligation, such as when we are required to provide information to law enforcement agencies by legal request; or our processing is in TrainDriver\'s legitimate interests, such as for Development, operation, protection and improvement of the Website, Application and/or Services, and the protection of the rights and interests of TrainDriver - 91免费版s. \nIf you have any questions or concerns about our processing of your personal data, or wish to exercise your rights, please feel free to contact us through customer service. \nJ. Changes\nWe reserve the right to modify or update this policy at any time. We will notify you of any such modifications or updates by sending you a notice via our Site and App. By continuing to use our Services after any modification or update, you agree to be bound by the modified or updated policy. We recommend that you review this policy regularly for the latest information. \nK. Questions about this Policy\nIf you have any questions about the content of this Privacy Policy or our practices, or wish to exercise your rights, please feel free to contact us.',
